# The read walk `for(&xs, …)` (B7a) lets its body READ the walked collection,
# so the body can share its handle (`h := xs`) and grow it through the share.
# The loop's guard holds `xs`'s runtime borrow flag, so the push panics
# instead of reallocating the buffer under the live element reference `x`.
# A user wrapper whose `walk_ref` forwards into an inner collection is NOT
# covered by the flag:
# issues/2026-10-24-a-forwarded-walk-leaves-the-inner-collection-unguarded.md.
stdout_keep_match=panic: container operation while an interior reference.*
timeout=300
